course: dictionary
lesson: 1578
title: One name, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names. A name with a capital letter, like Charon, points to one special person, place or thing. The same name can point to different things, so context tells you which one is meant. The words around it are the clues.
explain: «Charon rowed the souls of the dead across the river Styx» has rowing, souls and the underworld in it, so Charon must be a ferryman in an old Greek story. «Pluto's biggest moon Charon is about half Pluto's width» has moon, Pluto and width in it, so this Charon is a moon in space. Ask yourself: what do the clue words point to?
explain: Check your meaning by putting it back in the sentence. If you say «Charon is a moon» in the first sentence, it stops making sense, so you know you have picked the wrong meaning.
fact: Charon is a proper noun, so it starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Charon» means the ferryman in ancient Greek stories who rowed the souls of the dead across the river Styx (or Acheron) into the underworld, in return for a coin.
fact: «Charon» also means the largest moon of the dwarf planet Pluto, about half Pluto's size.
fact: Ancient Greeks sometimes put a coin with the dead, to pay Charon for the crossing.
fact: Pluto and Charon are so close in size that they circle around a point between them, almost like a double planet.
exercise: «Charon rowed the souls of the dead across the river Styx.» Who is Charon in this sentence? | *A ferryman in an ancient Greek story | A type of small boat | A famous Greek runner | A moon of the dwarf planet Pluto
exercise: «Pluto's biggest moon Charon is about half Pluto's width.» What is Charon in this sentence? | A river | A ferryman | *A moon | A coin
exercise: Find and copy the word in «Pluto's biggest moon Charon is about half Pluto's width» that tells you Charon is a moon. | Pluto's | width | *moon | half
test: Why does Charon start with a capital C in both meanings? | Because it is a very important word | Because it is the name of a town | Because it is always the first word of a sentence | *Because it is a name, a proper noun
test: In «Charon rowed the souls of the dead across the river Styx», which clue shows the story meaning? | *Rowed the souls of the dead | Circle a point between them | Biggest moon | Half Pluto's width
exam: Read «Pluto and Charon are so close in size that they circle around a point between them.» Which meaning of Charon is it? | The ferryman of the ancient Greek stories | A Greek word for a small boat | *The moon of the dwarf planet Pluto | A coin for the dead
